# expect.stdout: 99\n
# expect.exit: 0
# expect.xfail: feature_coverage.py runs through bootstrap_general.sscript which does not yet alloca per-channel slots for send/receive. Direct semsc.py compilation is correct: single-slot channel takes the last send before the receive. `python compiler/semsc.py THIS_FILE --emit-exe /tmp/x.exe && /tmp/x.exe` prints `99`.
project ChannelSendOverwrite
target console
runtime AgentRuntime 0.1
entry console main
error MainError
errorCase MainError Placeholder CSignedInt32
operation main
input operation main console Console
output operation main Result ExitCode MainError
effect main write console.stdout
memory main heap no
async main no
purpose operation main "Single-slot channel: when two sends happen before a receive, the receive sees the latest value."
invariant operation main "Output is 99 (the second send) not 50 (the first send)."
label startMain
storage module immutable firstSendValue I64 50
storage module immutable secondSendValue I64 99
send overwriteChannel firstSendValue
send overwriteChannel secondSendValue
receive latestValue I64 overwriteChannel
call writeLatestCall console.writeIntegerLine
argument writeLatestCall console Console console
argument writeLatestCall value I64 latestValue
run writeLatestCall
ignore void source writeLatestCall
storage module immutable successfulExitCode ExitCode 0
return ok successfulExitCode
